      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 20, \"items_by_type\": {\"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_4405\", \"desc\": \"For each combination of activity and department/academic year enrollment statistics, list the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, category description, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the category name and ordered by the category name, along with the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects offered (subject count), minimum number of total units for those subjects, and the average number of enrolled students per subject (for departments and academic years where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 5). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2958\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1350\", \"desc\": \"For each department and school, provide the department name, school name, the average, range, and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, and the total enrolled students, considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with at least one enrolled student. Additionally, for each school, include a grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (null department name, school name, nulls for statistics, and total enrolled students). For students whose first name is 'Peter' and who are in the Mathematics department, also show their last name, email address, student year, and the minimum department budget code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's full name, as well as the department full name and department last activity date. The results include all these columns in the following order: department name, school name, average enrolled students, range of enrolled students, variance of enrolled students, total enrolled students, last name, email address, student year, windowed minimum department budget code, department full name, and department last activity date. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2272\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3311\", \"desc\": \"For each course that has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', list the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, reserve catalog key, and the dense rank over the material status key ordered by material status key, along with the department name, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units of courses offered by that department (considering only courses offered this year with non-null total units). Present the results ordered by course number and course number description. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4683\", \"desc\": \"For each department where the total number of subject enrollments for subjects offered in the current term is greater than 10, and for each course number in that department where the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2, provide the department name, the total number of subject enrollments, the course number, the number of unique library subjects offered, the minimum total units for those subjects, and the name of the responsible faculty member for each course. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3078\", \"desc\": \"For each subject title and department name where the total units are greater than 3, give the number of offered sections, the minimum number of enrolled students, and the average lab units for those subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4724\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the library in the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Additionally, for the corresponding offering department and school, provide the number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ' and the minimum total units for those subjects. Also, include the department phone number and the school name for the offering department, and display the responsible faculty name for each subject. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, maximum total units for each row and the next two rows, number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ', minimum total units for those subjects, department phone number, school name, and responsible faculty name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4812\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 combinations of department name, subject code, and course number (where the department is degree granting and the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2) with the highest number of unique library subjects offered, display the department name, subject code, number of subject codes, minimum department budget code, course number, number of unique library subjects offered, minimum total units, the subject title with the most enrolled students for that course, and the corresponding number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3235\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and its corresponding facility organization key where the department is in the Provost Area, provide the number of organizations, the minimum department hierarchy level 3 code, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of HR organization units per facility organization (considering only those with a non-null DLC key and where the hierarchy type is 'Standard Hierarchy'), listing the results in order by department name and facility organization key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2151\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4515\", \"desc\": \"For each department, academic year, activity title, and sponsor name where the subject enrollment number is greater than 10 and the maximum enrollment for the activity is greater than 10, provide the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, activity title, sponsor name, number of unique activities, minimum fee, and the sponsor type. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3644\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a total of 1 unit, show the subject title from the summary, the course number from the offered table, the subject title from the offered summary, the department name from the summary, the offer department name from the offered summary, the row number within each department name group ordered by subject title from the summary, and for each department, also provide the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student). List the results ordered by department name and row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1165\", \"desc\": \"For each subject where the responsible faculty MIT ID in the library subject offered table is 928034000 or the number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table is greater than 5, and where the offer department name in the tip subject offered table is either 'Chemistry' or 'Biology', show the subject title from the library subject offered table, the offer department name from the tip subject offered table, the term code from both tables, the number of enrolled students from both tables, and the minimum number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table over each master subject ID group. Additionally, for the department offering the subject, show the department name, the range of enrolled students, and the variance of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department, considering only departments that grant degrees, courses that are at the graduate level, and excluding the Biology department. Present the results ordered by subject title and department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1335\", \"desc\": \"List, for each department, either (a) the department's full name, the range and variance of the total units for degree-granting Mathematics department courses offered in the 2008 academic year along with the long course description for each course (with the reason 'Math 2008 Stats'), or (b) the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units) where the average total units is greater than the overall average across all departments (with the reason 'High Avg Units'). Show the columns in the following order: department name, total units range, total units variance, average total units, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, long course description, and reason for inclusion. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3590\", \"desc\": \"Show, for each subject, the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the school code and ordered by school code for subjects where the school code is not null and the subject title is not null; and for subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a cluster type of 'S', show the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED, the offer department name, the total units from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the subject title. Indicate the source of each row as either 'Subq1' or 'Subq2'. List all results together, showing the columns: subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, dense rank by school, offer department name, total units, row number window, and source, in that order, ordered by subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3867\", \"desc\": \"For each subject in a department where the school code and subject title are not null, and for each subject offered in the 2022FA term with total units greater than the average for that term, display the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, the number of subjects in the same department, the subject ID, the term description, and the running sum of total units for that academic year, ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4197\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term with term code '2012SU' that also has a cluster type of 'S', show the subject title, offer department name, offer school name, cluster type description, the difference between the number of enrolled students for that subject and the average number of enrolled students for all subjects in the same department in that term, the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the number of enrolled students, and the deviation of the number of enrolled students from the average number of enrolled students for that department in that term as calculated from the summary table. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, offer department name, offer school name, cluster type description, deviation from department average (from the first calculation), window column (dense rank), and deviation from department average (from the summary calculation). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
