RDER BY DEPARTMENT_NAME).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` is consumed by enrollment-dispersion metrics per department (`dw_1350`, `dw_1165`, `dw_1689`, `dw_4640`, `dw_3356`, `dw_4527`), always joined to a department dimension on `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`, and serves \"per-department enrollment statistics\" question patterns.\n- `SIS_DEPARTMENT` is the canonical dimension whenever `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`, school, or budget attributes are needed (concept decision guide; used in `dw_1474`, `dw_1350`, `dw_1165`, `dw_4527`, `dw_3356`, `dw_2151`).\n- `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY` serves subject-count/total-enrollment rollups (`dw_4527`, `dw_4650`, `dw_3727`, `dw_1474`); `SUBJECT_SUMMARY` serves official enrollment-number questions (`dw_4812`, `dw_4683`).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- Retrieved full details (`semantic_get`): `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `SIS_DEPARTMENT`, `STUDENT_DEPARTMENT`, `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE`, `SUBJECT_SUMMARY`, `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY`, `column_concept_enrollment_measures`, `concept_department_dimension`, `column_concept_department_name`, and metrics `dw_1335`, `dw_1350`, `dw_1165`, `dw_1689`, `dw_4640`, `dw_2958`, `dw_4527`, `dw_3356`, `dw_1474`, `dw_2151`, `dw_4650`, `dw_3727`, `dw_4231`, `dw_1049`.\n- Discovery-only entities judged related but not central (IAP_*, FCLT_*, HR_*, MASTER_DEPT_*, SPACE_*, MOIRA_*, time dimensions, catalog feeds): their descriptions confirm they carry no `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`-per-subject + degree-granting combination relevant to this task; discarded per screening rules.\n- `mysql_query` verification: **attempted 12+ times; every call failed with `1045 Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`** — the database was unreachable for this session, so runtime verification could not be performed. The SQL below is constructed strictly from precedent SQL patterns retrieved from the semantic network.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns**: `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` (measure `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, count key `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY`, join key `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`) joined to `SIS_DEPARTMENT` (`DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`).\n\n**6b. SQL approach**: Two CTEs — (1) Avg/Var branch: `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y' AND DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Political Science'`, computing `AVG`, `VARIANCE`, and `COUNT(TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY)` grouped by `DEPARTMENT_NAME`; (2) CoeffVar branch: `DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Chemistry'` (no degree-granting filter, per the question's wording), computing `STDDEV(...)/NULLIF(AVG(...),0)` and the same count. UNION ALL with NULLs in non-applicable measure columns and literal reason labels, ordered by department name — exactly the `dw_1335` union shape. Bare `STDDEV()` per the tip. No rounding.\n\n**6c. Reasons**:\n- *Data*: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED is at subject-per-term grain (no section fan-out); `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`→`DEPARTMENT_CODE` is a many-to-one join to the department dimension (no duplication); `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` physically exists (verified via column definitions).\n- *Semantic-network*: `column_concept_enrollment_measures` decision guide routes \"number of enrolled students … per department totals\" to `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`; `concept_department_dimension` routes degree-granting filters to `SIS_DEPARTMENT`.\n- *Business*: 3 avg/variance precedents + the single coefficient-of-variation precedent (`dw_4640`) + 2 variance/stddev precedents all use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED for this exact question shape; `dw_1335` establishes the reason-column UNION pattern.\n\n**6d. Alternatives**: `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY` would satisfy all requirements with fuller registrar coverage; the tie-breaker is precedent frequency — every retrieved precedent combining \"degree-granting\" + \"enrolled students\" dispersion statistics uses TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, so I follow it. (Could not be empirically tie-broken via join-match rates because the database was inaccessible.)\n\n",
